  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo></math>. be an A.P. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, the product <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> is minimum and the sum of its first <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> terms is zero then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></msub></math> is equal to"
  },
